<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.Ayatsuri2D.Ayatsuri2D</id>
  <name>Ayatsuri2D</name>
  <summary>Rig, animate and run Live2D-style 2D models</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.ayatsuri2d">
    <name>Ayatsuri2D</name>
  </developer>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-only AND MIT AND Apache-2.0</project_license>
  <description>
    <p>
      Ayatsuri2D is an open, native 2D puppet studio. Import artwork from
      Photoshop or Krita, mesh and rig it, add physics and expressions,
      animate it, and export Cubism-compatible moc3 models for apps like
      VTube Studio.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Imports layered PSD, Krita and Clip Studio Paint artwork, and Cubism moc3 and cmo3 models</li>
      <li>Automatic and hand-edited meshes, with Mirror Edit</li>
      <li>Warp and rotation deformers, blend shapes and keyed parameters</li>
      <li>Physics with a live pendulum preview, expressions and motions</li>
      <li>An animation timeline, with video export through ffmpeg when installed</li>
      <li>Pen tablet pressure on Linux and macOS</li>
      <li>A local WebSocket API for tracking apps and tools</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Live2D and Cubism are trademarks of Live2D Inc. Ayatsuri2D is an
      independent project and is not affiliated with it.
    </p>
  </description>
